      "content": "# Display Starting Position\nControl",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 237,
      "topLeftY": 179,
      "bottomRightX": 384,
      "bottomRightY": 281,
      "content": "The horizontal and vertical\ndisplay starting points on the\nTV screen are determined by\nspecifying the position at\nwhich the black background\ndisplay begins. This is done\nwith the values of addresses\nHP5 to HP0 and VP5 to VP0\nas shown in Fig. 6 and Fig. 7.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 237,
      "topLeftY": 290,
      "bottomRightX": 389,
      "bottomRightY": 336,
      "content": "The horizontal starting position\nHS and the vertical start\nposition VS may be found\nusing the following equations:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 237,
      "topLeftY": 337,
      "bottomRightX": 382,
      "bottomRightY": 372,
      "content": "HS = T × 4 [2⁵ × HP5 + 2⁴ ×\nHP4 + 2³ × HP3 + 2² × HP2²\n+ 2 × HP1 + HP0) + P]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 237,
      "topLeftY": 376,
      "bottomRightX": 387,
      "bottomRightY": 412,
      "content": "VS = H × 4 (2⁵ × VP5 + 2⁴ ×\nVP4 + 2³ × VP3 + 2² × VP2 + 2 ×\nVP1 + VP0)",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 237,
      "topLeftY": 415,
      "bottomRightX": 389,
      "bottomRightY": 496,
      "content": "where: P = width of character,\nfrom Table 4;\nT = 1/fc [fc = oscillating\nfrequency; 6MHz typ.]\nH = period of horizontal\nsynchronization signal\n[63.5μs typ.]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
